{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "NewsBroadcaster Plugin Architecture Tour",
  "description": "A guided walkthrough of the single-file Rust/Oxide plugin (v2.0.0) for a new maintainer: state model, config migration, the broadcast pipeline, UI generation, and the optional integrations it must degrade gracefully without.",
  "ref": "main",
  "steps": [
    {
      "directory": ".",
      "title": "One File, Whole Plugin",
      "description": "Situation: `NewsBroadcaster.cs` (~3400 lines) is the entire plugin. `PLUGIN_DOCS.md` is the admin/API reference, `CODEFLING_DESCRIPTION.md` is store copy, `previews/` holds rendered screenshots.\n\nThere is no server here, but `tools/test-harness/run.sh` compiles the plugin as C# 6/7 against .NET Framework 4.8 with stand-ins for the Oxide/Rust APIs, runs ~125 functional checks and can render every screen to PNG. A real server reload (`oxide.reload NewsBroadcaster`) is still the final check."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "line": 22,
      "title": "Plugin Identity & Optional Integrations",
      "description": "The `[Info]` attribute (line 17) carries the version (`2.0.0`) — bump it together with `PLUGIN_DOCS.md`.\n\n`[PluginReference]` wires up `ImageLibrary`, `Notify`, `ServerRewards`, `Economics` as *optional* plugins. Every call site null-checks and `IsLoaded`-checks them: a server without ServerRewards still broadcasts news fine, just without point payouts."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 45,
          "character": 0
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 60,
          "character": 0
        }
      },
      "title": "Per-Player State Lives in Parallel Dictionaries",
      "description": "Everything keyed by `ulong` SteamID: open UI, auto-close and toast timers, `editors` (an `EditorSession` per admin: draft + toggles), read-reward timers, bulk selections, like cooldowns, `openPopups` (which post a popup shows and where it was opened from), archive pages and the once-per-session reminder set.\n\nGotcha: there is no player session object. A new dictionary needs a matching removal in `OnPlayerDisconnected` and `Unload` — the test suite checks every one by name.\n\n`dataDirty`/`saveTimer` drive the debounced save path (next steps)."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 96,
          "character": 0
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 112,
          "character": 0
        }
      },
      "title": "The Announcement Record",
      "description": "`Announcement` is the one data shape everything revolves around: stored in `StoredData.Announcements`, rendered by every screen, sent to Discord and hooks.\n\n`LikedPlayers`/`ReadByPlayers`/`ReadRewardedPlayers`/`LikeRewardedPlayers` are per-post sets of SteamIDs — read tracking (NEW badges) and reward-once logic live here. `EditedDate` was added in 2.0.0; missing fields simply default on old data."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 600,
          "character": 0
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 655,
          "character": 0
        }
      },
      "title": "Config Migration Happens Before Deserialization",
      "description": "`LoadConfig` reads the raw `JObject` first and patches it (`MigrateLegacyRewardArrays`), injects the default themes if none exist, validates/clamps values, and finally re-saves when the file lacks keys added in newer versions (the `DeepEquals` check).\n\nImplication: for a schema change, add a JObject-level migration here, or existing servers silently lose settings on upgrade."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 879,
          "character": 0
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 916,
          "character": 0
        }
      },
      "title": "Two Save Paths: Immediate vs Debounced",
      "description": "`SaveAnnouncements()` writes the data file at once — used for admin actions and whenever a reward was paid (so a crash cannot pay twice). It also trims to `MaxStoredAnnouncements`, keeping pinned posts first and firing `OnNewsDeleted` for dropped ones.\n\n`MarkDataDirty()` is for high-frequency, low-value updates (likes, read marks, last-seen): it flips `dataDirty` and arms a 15 s timer. `OnServerSave` and `Unload` flush anything pending."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "line": 1067,
      "title": "Cleanup Mirrors the State Dictionaries",
      "description": "`OnPlayerDisconnected` is the teardown checklist for the dictionaries from the Fields step. `Init()` (line 837) is the mirror image at startup: register permissions, then `LoadAnnouncements()` repairs old data (null sets, duplicate ids) and sorts newest-first so index 0 is always the latest post.\n\n`OnPlayerSleepEnded` (line 999) shows the newest unseen post and sends the 'N unread' reminder once per session."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1090,
          "character": 0
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 1131,
          "character": 0
        }
      },
      "title": "The Broadcast Pipeline",
      "description": "`CreateAnnouncement` → insert at index 0 → `SaveAnnouncements()` → register the image with ImageLibrary → `OnNewsBroadcast` hook. Both `news.show` (line 1133) and the editor's save button go through it, then `SendToDiscord` and `NotifyPlayers`.\n\n`NotifyPlayers` shows a toast (or the popup when toasts are disabled) to every viewer, never forces a popup over an open NewsBroadcaster screen, and marks the post as seen so respawning doesn't show it again."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "line": 1294,
      "title": "Player Entry Point: /news",
      "description": "The chat command dispatches `latest`, `admin` (admins only), `help`, and otherwise opens the archive (`ShowHistory`). Everything else players do is a console command bound to a CUI button (`news.view`, `news.like`, `news.page`)."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "line": 1998,
      "title": "CUI Is Built Fresh, Every Time",
      "description": "`ShowPopup` is representative: tear down (`DestroyUI`), then build a `CuiElementContainer` with hand-computed anchors — always via `Anchor()`/`F()` so floats are culture-invariant.\n\nTwo exceptions avoid rebuilds: `AddLikeButton` (line 1987) swaps just the heart so the reader keeps their scroll position, and editor text input doesn't rebuild the editor so fields keep focus.\n\n`PopupOrigin` decides the footer button (archive / back to archive / back to editor), auto-close (broadcasts only) and read tracking (never for previews)."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "line": 2570,
      "title": "Admin Screens",
      "description": "`ShowAdminList` (rows with RESEND / PIN / EDIT / DEL and bulk selection), `ShowEditor` (line 2873: type chips, option toggles, preview) and `ShowThemeSelection` share the same admin colours (`AdminSurface`, `AdminSurfaceRaised`, …). Admin button commands get the caller through `AdminPlayer(arg)`, which returns null for non-admins."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "line": 3261,
      "title": "Rewards: Optional Plugins, Once Per Player",
      "description": "`GiveRewards` creates items directly (dropping them at the player's feet when the inventory is full), adds ServerRewards points with a plain `ulong` id (newer Rust wraps `userID`, which ServerRewards can't read), and deposits Economics currency.\n\n`CanGrantRewardBundle` checks everything first; if a needed plugin is missing nothing is paid and nothing is recorded, so the reward can be paid later."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "line": 3379,
      "title": "Discord Is Fire-and-Forget",
      "description": "`SendToDiscord` is a no-op unless the webhook is configured. `webrequest.Enqueue` posts asynchronously and only logs failures — a bad webhook never breaks a broadcast. `allowed_mentions` lets only the configured `RoleMention` ping (`@everyone`/`@here` are allowed only when that setting contains them)."
    },
    {
      "file": "NewsBroadcaster.cs",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 536,
          "character": 0
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 553,
          "character": 0
        }
      },
      "title": "The Public Hook Contract",
      "description": "`BuildHookData` is the payload for every `Interface.CallHook` (`OnNewsBroadcast`, `OnNewsEdited`, `OnNewsDeleted`, `OnNewsRead`, `OnNewsLiked`). Other plugins depend on these exact keys — renaming or dropping one is a breaking change; adding keys is fine."
    },
    {
      "title": "Where to Go From Here",
      "description": "You now have the map: state dictionaries and their cleanup, config migration, the two save modes, the broadcast pipeline, and the CUI patterns.\n\nFor a UI change start from `ShowPopup`/`ShowHistory`/`ShowAdminList`, then run `tools/test-harness/run.sh previews` and look at the PNGs. For a data change start from `Announcement` and add a test in `tools/test-harness/Harness/Tests.cs`."
    }
  ]
}
